ore[/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-fast-loop[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-fast-loop: in sase-core, unify dependency features with a [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cargo-hakari workspace-hack plus a tool-free check.sh features gate [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF](also run in CI). Add `just fast`, and make rust-version true by [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]deleting the incompatible_msrv allows. Measure a ≤5 s no-edit -p scope [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]switch.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]sase-core agent guide, provider shims, module map, README[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core-agent-guide[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core-fast-loop[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core-agent-guide: rewrite sase-core AGENTS.md to the target content, add[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]CLAUDE.md and GEMINI.md import shims, add `just modules` and fill the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]missing top-level `//!` summaries. Delete the stale sase_core_py binding[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]manifest and cut the README down to current facts.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]repo-open AGENTS.md hint, sase_repo skill, core memory fix[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]instruction-delivery[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]instruction-delivery: sase repo open names an opened repo's AGENTS.md on[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stderr, the sase_repo skill says the same, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]rust_core_backend_boundary core memory stops pointing at ../sase-core [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and points at docs/rust_backend.md (sase-15w). Also add a short [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]cross-repo pointer in docs/rust_backend.md.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Core pin ratchet workflow opens its PR[/bold #D7AFFF]                        [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]pin-ratchet-bot[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]pin-ratchet-bot: make core-pin-ratchet.yml tolerate the apply path's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]exit 2 so it reaches the push and PR steps. Behavior-test the step [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]script (sase-15v).[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Dev extension rebuilds when linked sase-core source changes[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]extension-freshness[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]extension-freshness: rust-install stamps the source identity (HEAD plus [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]a dirty digest) it built from. validate_test_environment compares it [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]with the linked checkout and flags a rebuild through a new status bit [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and fingerprint bucket, _setup rebuilds on that bit, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]stale-extension flake-baseline entry is retired.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Managed-tmp reaper covers the root agents actually use[/bold #D7AFFF]        [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]reaper-root[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]reaper-root: capture SASE_TMPDIR (and sibling SASE path overrides) in [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the service env, and warn when the reaper's managed root differs from [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the launch root, so per-run cargo targets are really reaped (sase-15q). [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]This is a prerequisite for larger incremental target dirs.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Incremental check/clippy through the athena rustc wrapper[/bold #D7AFFF]     [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]incremental-check[dim] · [dim][/dim]after reaper-root[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]incremental-check: sase-rustc-wrapper runs metadata-only incremental [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]units directly and strips incremental from codegen units before sccache,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]and chezmoi drops incremental=false. A new sase config opt-in replaces [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the forced CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 and athena enables it. Measure a ≤30 s [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]edit→check.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-165","llm_provider":"muse","model":"muse-spark-1.3-contributor","patch_name":"gh_sase-org__sase","phase_bead_id":"sase-165.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-4f7e2d3524cd3c0867687c63291b4b11","started_at":"2026-09-22T13:12:42.497601+00:00","state":"active"},{"capabilities":{"durably_revivable":true,"historically_viewable":true,"missing_requirements":[],"restartable":true},"commits":[{"committed_at":1790097350,"sha":"8d085d03c641a4904a06433bca64619e0cd45472","subject":"fix: widen dev-extension freshness identity INPUT_PATHS to Cargo.toml, Cargo.lock, rust-toolchain.toml and crates/"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"3988e37780f6579b825ce97d61cd1afcabeb8e89693ad1febab7f235b1c03376","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-165.land--1/chat.md","size_bytes":10165},"commits":{"digest":"25e60d625c367a71881a4a5f9d7a0f81675ce2b62ae1487a698a0f63f6fd265f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-165.land--1/commits.json","size_bytes":292},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"e5b9fa24e45ad09d96fe04998c08ed4f9995d685d7898351da13de1433ac162d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-165.land--1/embedded_workflows.json","size_bytes":68},"meta":{"digest":"a66c3371ef9beb29f698f63ce37be264723ffb114ca51fdb920fc7dbf05cf9a9","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-165.land--1/meta.json","size_bytes":677},"prompt":{"digest":"ee5b63a1ae69fbf9a753fff6abfd0067c1756d00004a4048d918a32dab7b4339","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-165.land--1/prompt.md","s